"""Turn OFF core's substitute "Generated by Odoo" PDF for UBL purchase imports
— on a core that has such a thing.

WHAT IT SETS. The system parameter `account_edi_ubl_cii.disable_pdf_in_xml` to
`True`. Core reads it at
`account_edi_ubl_cii/models/account_edi_ubl.py:3924` and, when it is set, returns
at :3926-3932 without rendering anything.

WHY IT EXISTS. On a UBL purchase import with no main attachment yet, core renders
a QWeb PDF, watermarks it "Generated by Odoo" (:3950), names it
"<invoice> - Generated by Odoo.pdf" (:3955-3958) and claims
`message_main_attachment_id` with `force=True` (:3965). On a test bill
the substitute attachment held the slot while the vendor's own PDF, attached
later, did not — the id order shows core ran first.

🔴 CONDITIONAL SINCE 19.0.3.10.0, AND THE CONDITION IS MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED.
This script used to write the parameter unconditionally and call that
idempotence. *(measured on a legacy-core test copy)* upgrading this
module from an earlier fork at 19.0.1.1.3 therefore left
`account_edi_ubl_cii.disable_pdf_in_xml = True` on a core whose
`account_edi_ubl_cii` does not contain the string `disable_pdf_in_xml` anywhere
and ships no `data/ir_config_parameter_data.xml` at all. That row is the exact
thing the dual-core design forbids: it reads like a decision and does nothing, and the next
person to wonder why no substitute PDF appears will read it and stop looking.

The decision now lives in ONE place,
`account.move._ai_apply_substitute_pdf_policy`, shared with `post_init_hook`.
Read that method for why the gate is a registry capability and not the core
profile, and not `env.ref` either — the database says YES on the legacy bench,
because the xmlid outlived the core that declared it.

🔴 THE TRADE-OFF, BECAUSE THIS IS A GLOBAL SWITCH AND THE MODULE FIX IS NOT.
Setting this parameter disables the substitute PDF for EVERY UBL purchase import
in the database, including a genuine Peppol e-invoice that arrives as XML only
and therefore has nothing human-readable in it — which is precisely the case core
wrote that feature for. The US deployment takes that trade because its only producer of
UBL purchase documents is this module, which always starts from the vendor's own
PDF. A deployment with real inbound Peppol traffic — for example one with
`account_edi_finvoice`, `connector_apix` and the Peppol UBL stack installed —
would not want it, and on that deployment's core this script now writes nothing
at all.

WHY BOTH THIS AND THE ORDERING FIX. `ai.invoice.import._finalize_import` sets
the vendor's PDF as the move's main attachment BEFORE the decoder runs, which
makes core return early on its own `invoice.message_main_attachment_id` check.
That fix is the precise one, it is what puts the vendor's own PDF in the preview,
and it is correct on BOTH cores — inert where nothing competes for the slot.
This parameter is the blunt backstop for any path the hook point does not reach
(a re-import, the email route, a future caller). Neither is redundant.

WHY A MIGRATION RATHER THAN A DATA FILE. Core ships the record in
`account_edi_ubl_cii/data/ir_config_parameter_data.xml` inside `<data
noupdate="1">` with the value `False`. `noupdate` means a later core upgrade will
NOT reset whatever value the database holds, so writing it once from a migration
sticks — and we do not have to own a data file that fights core's forever.

IT RUNS ONCE PER DATABASE, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. A database crosses
19.0.3.1.0 exactly once, so an administrator who later sets the switch back to
False keeps it. A module that re-asserted a global policy at every upgrade would
be overruling the person who runs it, forever.
"""

import logging

from odoo import SUPERUSER_ID, api

_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)


def migrate(cr, version):
    if not version:
        return

    env = api.Environment(cr, SUPERUSER_ID, {})
    written = env["account.move"]._ai_apply_substitute_pdf_policy()
    _logger.info(
        "goodahead_invoice_ai_import 19.0.3.1.0: substitute-PDF switch -> %s",
        "True" if written else "not written (this core does not read it)",
    )
